# Single Quotes Preference

- Use **single quotes** (`'`) for strings in `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.mjs`, and `.cjs`.
- In JSX attributes, also prefer single quotes: `className='mb-card'`, `title='Salvar'`.
- Keep **double quotes** only when required:
  - JSON files (`.json`) — JSON syntax requires double quotes.
  - Strings that contain a single quote and would need excessive escaping — use a template literal or escape instead.
- Run `npm run format` after bulk edits; Prettier enforces this via `.prettierrc` (`singleQuote: true`, `jsxSingleQuote: true`).

```tsx
// ✅
import { useAuth } from '@services';
const label = 'Salvar alterações';
<Button type='button'>{label}</Button>

// ❌
import { useAuth } from "@services";
const label = "Salvar alterações";
<Button type="button">{label}</Button>
```
